{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1788116103,"nonce":"RhLSvQ8MY7tUEHXDXZwOUHufW0I=","target":"f8369fa13c46692ead2c79f0017cd58e0dba6b3a56b364a9dc5e84bf426bdd3f","message":"AMENDMENT from spike 0.1 (FINDINGS.md, git-bug 3fa4cf5) — orchestrator, post-gate.\n\nBench facts this spec now inherits. Not a rewrite; the Scope and Acceptance stand.\n\n**Where the mod lives.** The repo root IS the AutoRimmer mod folder — About/,\nSource/AutoRimmer/, Assemblies/ at the root of `autorimmer/`, exactly as this\nspec already writes them and exactly like analyzerbridge/logrelay/Factions.\n`profile/make-profile-agent.sh` links `Mods/AutoRimmer -\u003e \u003crepo root\u003e` and\ncurrently reports it as the profile build's one MISSING source; creating\n`About/` is what clears it. (The spike script first pointed at `autorimmer/Mod`;\ncorrected in 57263e7 so the bench matches this spec rather than the reverse.)\n\n**packageId + load order.** Use `dorian.autorimmer`. The slot is already\nreserved: `profile/gen-modsconfig.py` LOAD_ORDER_TAIL ends\ndubsperformanceanalyzer -\u003e dorian.analyzerbridge -\u003e dorian.autorimmer, so\nAutoRimmer patches see the final state of the stack. Nothing to configure.\n\n**csproj reference path.** Assembly-CSharp lives at\n`_RimWorld-Agent/RimWorldLinux_Data/Managed/`. Note that `RimWorldLinux_Data`\nis a REAL directory of symlinked children (not a symlink), rebuilt by\nmake-profile-agent.sh on every run.\n\n**Isolation is not free, and it has a one-line assert.** A symlinked\n`RimWorldLinux` re-roots the whole game at the Steam install via\n`/proc/self/exe` and silently loads Steam's Mods/ instead of the bench's (~40\nTypeLoad red errors, nothing to do with the modlist). The profile now ships a\nreal copy of the stub. Any script or test that boots the bench should assert\nPlayer.log line 1 reads\n`Mono path[0] = '\u003c...\u003e/_RimWorld-Agent/RimWorldLinux_Data/Managed'`.\nOrchestrator verified this on an independent boot.\n\n**Liveness is not process-up.** Hyprland delivers no frames to a window on a\nhidden special workspace, and RimWorld's tick loop is frame-bound, so a parked\nbench sat at 1-2 fps ~= 4 tps while looking perfectly healthy in `ps`.\n`run-agent.sh` fixes it pre-launch (render_unfocused + misc:render_unfocused_fps\n+ vblank_mode=0). For this spec: `status.json` should carry enough for a caller\nto assert a TICK DELTA, not merely that the game is up. Orchestrator verified\n30.0 fps / 60 tps with the window hidden and focus never leaving the terminal.\n\n**Prefs the bench seeds, that this spec should not fight.** `runInBackground=True`\nis load-bearing (defaults False; `PrefsData.Apply()` overrides Root.Start a few\nframes in, and an unfocused bench freezes without it). Also devMode=True,\n`automaticPauseMode=Never`, `pauseOnLoad=False`, `pauseOnError=False` — the mod\nowns time, the game must not pause behind it.\n\n**The threading pattern is validated.** The spike built a throwaway\n`AutoRimmerSpike` mod on exactly the analyzerbridge shape (GameComponent +\nfiles-only watcher thread) and drove ~950K ticks through it without incident.\nCopy analyzerbridge with confidence; it is a proven fit for this bench.\n\n**Zero-red-errors has a known baseline: 0 errors / 9 warnings.** The 9 are\nenumerated and triaged in FINDINGS section 5 (SteamAPI.Init x1 by design;\nGuests Socio-Butterfly degradation x2; StaticConstructorOnStartup hygiene notes\nx6 across Guests/FSWA/RealisticGasses). Independently reproduced by the\norchestrator on a clean boot. Acceptance can diff against that set rather than\ndemanding literal silence.\n\n**batchmode is not the v1 path** (23 GlobalTextureAtlasManager NREs violate the\nerror gate) and writes no Player.log at all — logs go to stdout. Relevant only\nif anything here scrapes logs.","files":null}]}